WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.587
A warning can catch an attack, or interrupt a genuine task. SignalLab lets you explore

00:00:05.587 --> 00:00:09.312
both outcomes, then connect them to human centred security design.

00:00:09.312 --> 00:00:13.809
Before the results appear, choose a prediction. The distractors expose two

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:19.124
misconceptions: that both errors must decrease, or that a different warning rule makes

00:00:19.124 --> 00:00:21.168
the messages themselves more dangerous.

00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:26.784
At threshold four, three threats trigger warnings. One threat is missed. One genuine

00:00:26.784 --> 00:00:31.968
task is interrupted. These counts come from eight disclosed teaching messages, split

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.560
evenly between phishing and legitimate examples.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.048
Now lower the threshold to two. All four authored threats trigger warnings, but two

00:00:40.048 --> 00:00:44.752
genuine tasks are interrupted. Changing the threshold changes the decision rule; the

00:00:44.752 --> 00:00:46.320
message evidence stays fixed.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.832
Compare the two runs. Missed threats fall from one to zero, while false alarms rise from

00:00:51.832 --> 00:00:56.655
one to two. This is the central trade-off: catching more attacks may consume more

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:57.000
attention.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.030
Open a message trace. The selected example has three points for an unfamiliar service,

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:07.418
zero for a sensitive request, one for urgency, and zero for an unexpected task. The

00:01:07.418 --> 00:01:08.496
total is four.

00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:13.526
The score equals the threshold, so the interface warns. The authored ground truth then

00:01:13.526 --> 00:01:18.916
determines whether that warning is useful or unnecessary. A cue score by itself does not

00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:21.072
establish whether a message is legitimate.

00:01:21.072 --> 00:01:26.025
Next, hold the message fixed and change only the interface. A minimal notice offers

00:01:26.025 --> 00:01:30.979
little explanation. It asks the learner to work out which evidence matters and what

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:32.040
action to take.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.900
Actionable guidance names the relevant evidence and gives a practical next step. The

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.385
fictional destination differs from the known campus service. The warning explains that

00:01:41.385 --> 00:01:44.376
difference instead of relying on visual alarm alone.

00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:49.033
The destination inspector reveals the full address without opening it. This supports

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:53.691
recognition and inspection. It also makes an important distinction visible: a familiar

00:01:53.691 --> 00:01:57.960
display name does not authenticate the sender or the linked service.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:03.108
The fresh-case check records an action, a reason and confidence. Explanations wait until

00:02:03.108 --> 00:02:08.256
all three cases are completed. Requiring a reason helps reveal the learner’s thinking,

00:02:08.256 --> 00:02:11.424
rather than treating a lucky choice as understanding.

00:02:11.424 --> 00:02:16.255
The report separates first attempts from repeated practice. Recall hides the inbox, and

00:02:16.255 --> 00:02:21.087
previously missed ideas return when the learner reopens the app. Progress stays locally

00:02:21.087 --> 00:02:23.688
in the browser and can be exported.

00:02:23.688 --> 00:02:29.120
The research log records actual Scopus AI and NotebookLM use, source checks and

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.717
corrections. Machine classification accuracy was not treated as proof of student

00:02:33.717 --> 00:02:37.896
learning. Software checks and real human review are recorded separately.

00:02:37.896 --> 00:02:42.856
SignalLab makes a security decision visible, lets learners change it, and asks them to

00:02:42.856 --> 00:02:47.817
explain the result. Try the public simulator and inspect the source. Peer trials and

00:02:47.817 --> 00:02:51.360
course review remain pending; learning gains have not been measured.
